  "curriculum": "The 180 EC English-taught BSc comprises 150 EC of compulsory major and a 30 EC approved minor in semester four. There is no required specialisation. The first year combines health determinants, EU institutions, communicable and chronic disease, healthy environments and technology, academic writing, four methodology trajectory modules, philosophy and a single 6 EC statistics course. The third semester covers demography, ageing, migration, lifestyle and work, a conditional 1 EC excursion, methods and a paper. If the excursion is omitted, its 1 EC transfers to Lifestyle, Work and Health. The fourth-semester minor can be taken at Maastricht or another approved institution. It must be academic and avoid substantive duplication. The fifth semester includes health systems and policy, trajectory work, philosophy and a 6 EC thesis proposal. The sixth semester consists of the 30 EC Placement and Thesis, recorded under EPH3013 in the adopted EER.",
  "progression": "Year-two exams require 60 first-year EC for unconditional entry or at least 45 EC for conditional entry. Year three requires 120 EC for unconditional entry, or all year-one requirements and at least 42 year-two EC for conditional entry, subject to the exceptional provisions. Minor study abroad requires completing all first-year requirements. Required activities must be completed for exam access. The proposal precedes the semester-six placement and thesis. Placement approval rests with the coordinator on behalf of the Board of Examiners. The adopted EER specifies 16 weeks of total placement and thesis effort. The thesis is individual, with two examiners grading its content and the first examiner also grading the process. Each grade must reach 6.0. Detailed placement and thesis instructions sit in the programme learning environment.",
